<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional //EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd"> <html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office"> <head> <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8"> <title>Trump Doesn't Want You To Know This…</title></head> <body> <div>Trump messed up on stage once again. His staff was embarrassed and covered their faces&hellip;</div> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div><div> <div> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div> <a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" target="_blank"><img src="https://cdn.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" alt="HeaderLogo"></a> </div> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </div><div> <div> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div ><div><div><div><p>Trump messed up on stage once again.</p></div><table><tbody><tr><td><table><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><img src="https://cdn.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" alt="Donald Trump standing on a stage"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><div><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" target="_blank">&nbsp;</a></div><div><p>His staff was embarrassed and covered their faces…</p><p>This time his mental facilities failed him again.</p><p>What did he do exactly?</p><p>Trump slipped up and named the day the government will dump the US dollar</p><p>And bring in the new digital dollar system</p><p>That gives them full control over YOUR money.</p><p><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><strong><u>Get All The Details HERE&gt;&gt;&gt;&nbsp;</u></strong></a></p></div><div><p><i><strong>This is an advertisement.</strong></i></p><p><i>If you no longer wish to receive promotional messages from this advertiser, please unsubscribe below. Or write to: 5005 Lyndon B. Johnson Fwy. Suite 350 Dallas, TX 75244</i></p></div></div></div><div><div><hr><div>Ad by Brownstone Research</div><table><tbody><tr><td><table><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><img src="https://cdn.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" alt="Man sitting inside a Tesla Cybercab"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><div><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" target="_blank">&nbsp;</a></div><div><p>This man just got inside a Cybercab, Elon Musk’s new car that has no steering wheel or pedals.</p><p>What happens next will shock everyone.</p><p><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><strong><u>Click here to see this exclusive footage.&nbsp;</u></strong></a></p></div></div></div><div><div><div><strong>Sponsored Content</strong></div><div><div><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><strong><u>Only 3,000 FREE Gold Guides.&nbsp;</u></strong></a></div><div><i>Ad by <strong>Anchor Point Research</strong></i></div></div><div><div><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><strong><u>Why Does America Need a $250 Bill?&nbsp;</u></strong></a></div><div><i>Ad by <strong>Porter &amp; Company</strong></i></div></div><div><div><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><strong><u>This could be bigger than Tesla and SpaceX combined&nbsp;</u></strong></a></div><div><i>Ad by <strong>Brownstone Research</strong></i></div></div></div></div><div><div><hr><h1><strong>Why Goldman Sachs Views Grid and Utilities as the Key AI Growth Bottlenecks</strong></h1><p>Goldman Sachs warns that power infrastructure is emerging as the "forever bottleneck" for artificial intelligence, with a 2,600 GW grid interconnection backlog, 5-year connection delays, and $1.3 trillion in required utility CapEx threatening to slow AI model deployment.</p><table><tbody><tr><td><div><strong>Data Center Power Surge</strong></div><div><strong>+170% Demand</strong></div><div><strong>2025–2030 Global Growth (60% US)</strong></div></td><td><div><strong>US Interconnection Backlog</strong></div><div><strong>2,600 GW</strong></div><div><strong>Over 2x Total Installed Grid Capacity</strong></div></td></tr><tr><td><div><strong>Total AI Ecosystem CapEx</strong></div><div><strong>$7.6 Trillion</strong></div><div>Projected Spend 2026–2031</div></td><td><div><strong>Utility Sector Capital Plans</strong></div><div><strong>$1.3 Trillion</strong></div><div><strong>Required Spend 2026–2030</strong></div></td></tr></tbody></table><div><p>While advances in artificial intelligence models continue to accelerate, the physical infrastructure needed to power high-density computing clusters is falling behind. In a comprehensive research report, <strong>Goldman Sachs</strong> warned that electricity supply, grid interconnections, and utility capacity represent the defining friction point of the AI revolution, with global data center power consumption expected to <strong>surge 170% by 2030</strong>.</p><p>"Power is probably the forever bottleneck," emphasized Jason Tofsky, Global Head of Digital Infrastructure Investment Banking at Goldman Sachs. While aggregate AI-related capital expenditure across compute hardware, data centers, and power is forecast to reach <strong>$7.6 trillion between 2026 and 2031</strong>, physical development timelines operate on multi-year delays that software cycles cannot bypass.</p><div><p><strong>The Grid Interconnection Chokepoint:</strong> The U.S. interconnection queue currently carries 2,600 GW of proposed generation and storage—more than double the existing domestic grid. The median waiting time between application filing and commercial operation has stretched to five years, while lead times for high-voltage transformers and substations sit between three and five years.</p></div><h2><strong>Utility Re-Rating, Behind-the-Meter Power &amp; Execution Risks</strong></h2><p>The power deficit is restructuring relationships between tech giants, regulated utilities, and debt markets:</p><ul><li><strong>$1.3T Utility CapEx Supercycle:</strong> Regulated utilities are transitioning from defensive value investments to growth plays, requiring $1.3 trillion in capital spending through 2030 to build new generation, substations, and transmission lines.</li><li><strong>Behind-the-Meter &amp; Hybrid Solutions:</strong> To bypass congested queues, hyperscalers are exploring on-site generation, fuel cells, and microgrids. However, these alternatives face separate air-permitting hurdles and long environmental review periods.</li><li><strong>Community &amp; Local Pushback:</strong> Since January 2026, 86 large data center projects have been canceled or delayed, with 76 directly tied to community opposition regarding water consumption, emissions, and rising residential power bills.</li></ul><p>As hyperscaler debt issuance climbs toward $420 billion in 2027, the market advantage in the global AI race is increasingly shifting toward developers capable of securing verified power access and navigating grid delays.</p></div></div></div></div> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </div><div> <div> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div> <a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" target="_blank"><img src="https://cdn.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED" alt="FooterLogo"></a> </div> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </div><div> <div> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div ><p><span>Email sent by Systems and Technologies LLC, owner and operator of TrendWatchersLab.com</span></p><p><span>For assistance, contact: </span><a href="mailto:support@trendwatcherslab.com"><span>support@trendwatcherslab.com</span></a></p><p><span>© 2026 Trend Watchers Lab. All Rights Reserved.</span></p></div> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </div><div> <div> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div ><p><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><span><u>Privacy Policy</u></span></a></p></div> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> <table> <tbody><tr> <td> <div ><p><a href="https://app.cyberimpact.com/REDACTED"><span><u>Terms &amp; Conditions</u></span></a></p></div>